[h1]Server Guides[/h1]

[b]Publish your server's guides and rules, read in-game in a clean windowed viewer. Edit them live — straight from the pause menu, no relog, no file uploads.[/b]

Your rules and guides stop being a Discord link nobody opens and become a first-class, in-game window with a side menu and formatted text. Content lives in one folder on the server and is [b]streamed live[/b] to players: edit it and everyone sees the new version the next time they open the window. Built for dedicated / multiplayer servers — the client never touches the disk, it only receives text over the network.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]In-game guide & rules viewer[/b] — a window with a category menu on the left and formatted, scrollable text on the right.
[*][b]Live content[/b] — the guides live in a folder on the server; change them and players get the new version on reopen. No client downloads, no relog.
[*][b]Read-only for players[/b] — they open, read and close. No "I have read and agree" gate, no blocking.
[*][b]Rules auto-open[/b] — when you change the rules, the window pops up once for each player on their next join (tracked per character, by content hash).
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Edit in-game (staff only)[/h2]
Your staff never has to FTP into the server to fix a typo. Open the guide window and you get two extra buttons:
[list]
[*][b]Edit[/b] — edit the current page's text right there (the raw rich-text markup). Save, and the change is written on the server and goes live for everyone.
[*][b]Edit menu[/b] — create / rename / remove categories and pages, mark a category as [i]Rules[/i], and reorder — all from the UI. New pages get their file created automatically.
[/list]
[b]Who can edit is up to you[/b] — a sandbox option lists the access levels allowed (default [i]admin;moderator;overseer;gm[/i]; leave empty to allow none). The single-player / co-op host can always edit.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Multiplayer-ready[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Server-authoritative[/b] — only the server reads and writes the files. Every edit is re-validated on the server (access level, safe path, 256 KB limit); the buttons are cosmetic, a client can't forge a write.
[*][b]Streamed safely[/b] — pages are sliced into chunks over the network and reassembled on the client, so large guides just work.
[*][b]Live sync[/b] — saved edits broadcast to everyone; no relog.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Formatting & images[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Rich text[/b] — use the native [i]ISRichTextPanel[/i] tags: line breaks, font sizes, colors, alignment, indenting, images.
[*][b]Images[/b] — reference an image packed in a loaded mod's [i]media/[/i] folder by name. A demo image and a separate example image-mod are included so you can ship your own.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Setup[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Enable the mod on the server (and on clients in MP, via the Workshop).
[*]On first run it creates [i]~/Zomboid/Lua/ServerGuides/[/i] and fills it with template files — it never overwrites existing content.
[*]Edit the guides from inside the game, or edit the [i].txt[/i] files directly (UTF-8). Open the window from the [b]pause menu (Esc)[/b].
[/olist]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Sandbox options[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Access levels allowed to edit[/b] — a semicolon-separated list of roles that may edit in-game (default [i]admin;moderator;overseer;gm[/i]).
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Languages[/h2]
English and Português (Brasil).

[hr][/hr]
[i]Build 42. Safe to add to an existing server: it only creates its folder if missing and never overwrites your content.[/i]

[hr][/hr]
